  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the file set establishing the dependency graph for the Babel parser AST change:\n\n**Confirmed edge: Next.js \u2192 Babel** (direct, real)\n- `packages/next/src/bundles/babel/bundle.js` \u2014 `next` directly `require('@babel/parser')`, `require('@babel/types')`, `require('@babel/traverse')`, `require('@babel/generator')`, `require('@babel/core')`\n- `packages/next/package.json` devDependencies pin `@babel/parser@7.12.11`, `@babel/types@7.18.0`, `@babel/traverse@7.18.0`, `@babel/generator@7.18.0`, `@babel/core@7.18.0`\n- Root `package.json` `resolutions` re-pins the same four packages workspace-wide\n- `packages/next/taskfile-ncc.js` explains why these are devDependencies yet still ship: `@vercel/ncc` bundles them into `next/dist/compiled/*`, which is inside the `files` array of the published package \u2014 so despite living in `devDependencies`, they are vendored into the runtime artifact.\n\n**Expected edge that doesn't hold: webpack \u2192 Babel**\n- Root `package.json` lists `@babel/core` and `@babel/preset-react` only under `devDependencies` (alongside `babel-loader`), not `dependencies`.\n- `lib/javascript/JavascriptParser.js` \u2014 webpack's actual module parser `require(\"acorn\")`, not Babel.\n- `test/cases/parsing/precreated-ast/ast-loader.js` \u2014 webpack's \"precreated AST\" loader hook is acorn-shaped, confirming loaders don't hand webpack a Babel AST either.\n- So the Babel package is present only for webpack's own test fixtures (exercising `babel-loader`), not for anything the published `webpack` npm package executes.\n\n**Babel side**\n- `packages/babel-parser/package.json` and root `package.json` \u2014 identify `@babel/parser` as the origin package and the yarn-workspaces structure other babel packages (`@babel/traverse`, `@babel/types`) live in.\n\nThe retrieval task is complete \u2014 file selection only, no plan authored here.",
